WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.167
Sometimes one Data frame cell contains more than one value.

00:00:04.167 --> 00:00:11.207
For example, a customer may have several interests, a patient may have several diagnosis codes,

00:00:11.207 --> 00:00:14.217
or a document may have several tags.

00:00:14.217 --> 00:00:19.472
The explode method turns those list-like values into separate rows.

00:00:19.472 --> 00:00:26.407
In the example, Ava has two interests, Noah has one, and Mia has three.

00:00:26.407 --> 00:00:34.173
After exploding the interests column, each interest gets its own row while the customer name is repeated as needed.

00:00:34.748 --> 00:00:37.485
This structure is much easier to analyze.

00:00:37.485 --> 00:00:43.515
We can count interests, group by interest, or join the values with another table.

00:00:43.515 --> 00:00:47.385
Run the example and look at the value counts at the bottom.

00:00:47.385 --> 00:00:52.145
Then add another interest to one customer and run the code again.

00:00:52.145 --> 00:01:00.999
Explode is especially useful when data comes from JSON, APIs, or systems where one field can contain several items.
